From cf7064e0968a6fa632820b1197d98149584b6b78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolai Protasov <nprotaso@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:19:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Perf] [AMD] Qwen4-Exp HC: fused prefill hc_combine
 kernel

Fuse the HC combine with the next sublayer's per-branch grouped Gemma RMSNorm
into one JIT kernel (hc_combine_norm): the combined row stays in registers, so
the norm does not re-read it from HBM. GatedResidual.combine_and_normalize uses
it whenever no decode partials are present (prefill and other sites outside
SGLANG_OPT_QWEN4_FUSED_HC), and mix() takes the returned norm as its
normalized_input. The combined residual is bit-exact; the norm differs from
the unfused pair only in fp32 summation order.

Gated by SGLANG_ENABLE_HC_COMBINE_NORM_FUSION, default ON for HIP (measured
on gfx950 only) and OFF elsewhere.

Ported from 5e9bf8f2d6 ("prefill HC optimization") onto the upstream
combine_and_normalize / normalized_input HC API.
